 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Wheat for «حلالا طيبا» and for the feeding «إطعام», a seal for the oaths, an hourglass for the three days of fasting, geometric for «يبين الله». No people drawn (no ten poor, no slave). STAGING v4: 87-88 (lawful good things): believers in a market; palm plate on 87:6, two paths while the transgressors are named (87:15), a believer asks the seller (88:1) and pays on 88:5, with the wheat plate: lawfully earned food, no theft or usurpation (As-Sa'di). 89 (oaths): two men chat (unintended oaths in speech, Al-Muyassar), the man then makes a deliberate oath (89:10, seal); the friend leaves; a poor man comes and the man gives on 89:13 (feeding, wheat plate) and on 89:22 (clothing). One poor man stands for the needy: he is not a count of the ten. Freeing a slave (89:24-25) is not drawn. Hourglass for the three days of fasting; he bows on 89:37 (keeping oaths) and raises his hands on 89:45 (gratitude)."
 },
